     "body": "<p>We replaced some of the spring files in the default install with our own, to inject placeholders from central properties files and to add beans. We keep all of the fedora-persisted data in a separate high-level folder, such that we can replace the fedora binaries and configurations without wiping out data. How can the distribution make it easier to do configuration management on the implementation side? It will help if configuration is based more on distributed files and less on installer scripts.</p>",
